    "value": "Ox-bile (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sial/70168)\nciteturn21view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sial/70168\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: 【0†Skip to Content】\nL1: \nL2: US EN\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Image: Ox-bile, dehydrated, purified suitable for microbiology, extracted under controlled conditions from purified fresh bile】\nL5: \nL6: ### Key Documents\nL7: \nL8:   * 【2†COA】\nL9: \nL10:   * 【2†COO】\nL11: \nL12: 【2†View All Documentation】\nL13: \nL14: 70168\nL15: \nL16: 【3†Image: Millipore】\nL17: \nL18: Share\nL19: \nL20: # Ox-bile, dehydrated, purified\nL21: ## suitable for microbiology, extracted under controlled conditions from purified fresh bile\nL22: \nL23: Synonym(s):\nL24: \nL25: Bile acids sodium salt, cholic acid-deoxycholic acid sodium salt mixture\nL26: \nL27: 【4†Sign In】 to View Organizational & Contract Pricing.\nL28: \nL29: ### Select a Size\nL30: \nL31: Change View\nL32: \nL33: * * *\nL34: \nL35: ### About This Item\nL36: \nL37: NACRES:\nL38: \nL39: NA.85\nL40: \nL41: UNSPSC Code:\nL42: \nL43: 41106212\nL44: \nL45: Technical Service\nL46: \nL47: Need help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\nL48: \nL49: 【5†Let Us Assist】\nL50: \nL51: * * *\nL52: \nL53: * * *\nL54: \nL55: Properties\nL56: \nL57: ### Quality Segment\nL58: \nL59: 【6†100】\nL60: ### sterility\nL61: \nL62: non-sterile\nL63: \nL64: ### form\nL65: \nL66: powder\nL67: \nL68: ### impurities\nL69: \nL70: ~5% sodium chloride\nL71: \nL72: ### ign. residue\nL73: \nL74: ≤22% (as SO_{4})\nL75: \nL76: ### loss\nL77: \nL78: ≤8% loss on drying\nL79: \nL80: ### pH\nL81: \nL82: 6.0-9.2 (2% in H_{2}O)\nL83: \nL84: ### solubility\nL85: \nL86: distilled water: freely soluble\nL87: \nL88: ### application(s)\nL89: \nL90: microbiology\nL91: \nL92: Description\nL93: ### General description\nL94: \nL95: Ox-bileis a dehydrated, purified fresh bile which is used as a selective inhibitory agent in bile media. Ox-bile desiccated is prepared by a low temperature dehydration process which ensures a uniform product and eliminates the difficulties encountered in obtaining satisfactory supplies of fresh bile. An 8 to 10% solution of the dehydrated product is equivalent to fresh bile. 1 gram of dried Ox Bile is equivalent to 8 grams of fresh bile.\nL96: ### Application\nL97: Ox bile is used as a selective agent in culture media for selective growth of intestinal bacteria like E. coli, other feacal coliforms, feacal streptococci. But it is also used as a selective agent in media for detection of Yersinia enterocolitica, Aeromonas hydrophila and Vibrio species.\nL98: Bile salts may be used as one of the selective agents to prevent the growth of injured Escherichia coli cells, in an experiment done to identify the specific agent in the selective media which would inhibit the growth of the injured Escherichia coli ML30 cells. It may also be used for identification of isolates of Vibrio vulnificus (Beneckea) which is a halophilic bacterium, found responsible for causing several human infections.\nL99: * * *\nL100: \nL101: * * *\nL102: ## Safety Information\nL103: \nL104: ### Storage Class\nL105: \nL106: 11 - Combustible Solids\nL107: \nL108: ### WGK\nL109: \nL110: WGK 3\nL111: \nL112: ### Flash Point (°F)\nL113: \nL114: Not applicable\nL115: \nL116: ### Flash Point (°C)\nL117: \nL118: Not applicable\nL119: \nL120: ### PPE (personal protective equipment)\nL121: \nL122: Eyeshields, Gloves, type N95 (US)\nL123: \nL124: * * *\nL125: \nL126: ## Documentation\nL127: \nL128: Certificate of Analysis[Button: Certificate of Origin]\nL129: \nL130: * * *\nL131: \nL132: Choose from one of the most recent versions:\nL133: ### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\nL134: \nL135: Lot/Batch Number\nL136: \nL137: * * *\nL138: \nL139: Don't see the Right Version?\nL140: \nL141: If you require a particular version, you can look up a specific certificate by the Lot or Batch number.\nL142: \nL143: 【7†Search for a COA】\nL144: \nL145: ### Already Own This Product?\nL146: \nL147: Find documentation for the products that you have recently purchased in the Document Library.\nL148: \nL149: 【8†Visit the Document Library】\nL150: \nL151: * * *\nL152: \nL153: Related Categories\nL154: \nL155: 【9†Industrial Microbiology】\nL156: \nL157: 【10†Microbial Culture Media Raw Materials】\nL158: \nL159: * * *\nL160: \nL161: * * *\nL162: \nL163: Top\n"
